  "DECISIONS": [
    {
      "decidedBy": "Matthew Wrigley",
      "decidedOn": "2026-10-28",
      "decision": "Apply a payment to contributions first, then interest, then recovery costs, as NSW (PAYMENT_ALLOCATION_ORDER). A StrataVerze choice: the notes record no order.",
    },
    {
      "decidedBy": "Matthew Wrigley",
      "decidedOn": "2026-10-28",
      "decision": "Notice timing (NOTICE_RULES): each levy notice goes out 35 days before it falls due and is never given less than 14 days' notice, and a due date is never moved, because the decision to make the levy fixes it (STA s 100(4)(a)). Matthew Wrigley's StrataVerze decision of 28 Oct 2026: the STA and STGR set no notice rule, so these are StrataVerze choices, not rules of law.",
    },
    {
      "decidedBy": "Matthew Wrigley",
      "decidedOn": "2026-10-29",
      "decision": "2-lot quorum (MEETING_RULES.quorumNeedsEveryLot): at a general meeting of a 2-lot scheme, where the quorum needs both lots with no fallback (STA s 130(2), (4)), a count is refused unless both lots are recorded at the item, voting or abstaining, with a clear refusal and nothing written. Matthew Wrigley's StrataVerze decision of 29 Oct 2026.",
    },
  ],
  "DESIGNATED_STATUS": {
